# Command palette open-lag receipt, condition 3 of 4: PALETTE OPEN, row
# selection.
#
# The doc's receipt asks for row-selection keys as well as idle redraws. Rows
# are populated first (an empty actions lane would make the arrows a no-op and
# the sample a lie), and the measured block moves the selection only - no text
# changes, so `suggestion_runs` should stay at zero across it. Compare against
# palette_lag_open.scn: the difference between the two IS the cost of moving a
# selection.
#
# MEASURED BLOCK: the 10 down/up pairs below, 80 frames (each key is one frame
# and each `settle 2` is three, the countdown plus the step that sets it). The
# harness skips the one frame `log` costs and reads the 50 before it.
settle 30
key escape
open mere://alpha
open mere://beta
settle 20
assert visible
omnibar actions
type o
settle 20
assert omnibar open
assert suggestions >= 1
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
key down
settle 2
key up
settle 2
log palette lag: open row-selection sample complete
